Pattern selection and interpretation:
  -E, --extended-regexp         Match extended regular expressions.
  -F, --fixed-strings           Match literal strings.
  -G, --basic-regexp            Match basic regular expressions (default).
  -P, --perl-regexp             Use Perl-compatible expressions (PCRE2).
  -e, --regexp=PATTERNS         Add one or more search patterns.
  -f, --file=FILE               Read one pattern per line from FILE.
  -i, --ignore-case             Ignore case when matching (alias: -y).
      --no-ignore-case          Use case-sensitive matching (default).
  -w, --word-regexp             Require a whole word.
  -x, --line-regexp             Require a whole input line.
  -z, --null-data               Separate records with NUL instead of LF.

Miscellaneous:
  -s, --no-messages             Hide diagnostics for inaccessible files.
  -v, --invert-match            Select lines without a match.
  -V, --version                 Show the grep component version.
      --help                    Show this option list.
      --                        End option parsing.

Output control:
  -m, --max-count=NUM           Limit selected lines per input.
  -b, --byte-offset             Prefix results with their byte offset.
  -n, --line-number             Prefix results with their line number.
      --line-buffered           Flush output after each line.
  -H, --with-filename           Prefix every result with its file name.
  -h, --no-filename             Omit the file name prefix.
      --label=LABEL             Use LABEL as the name of standard input.
  -o, --only-matching           Print each nonempty match separately.
  -q, --quiet, --silent         Suppress output; stop at the first match.
      --binary-files=TYPE       Choose binary, text or without-match.
  -a, --text                    Read binary input as text.
  -I                            Skip matches in binary input.
  -d, --directories=ACTION      Directory handling: read, skip or recurse.
  -D, --devices=ACTION          Device and FIFO handling: read or skip.
  -r, --recursive               Search directories recursively.
  -R, --dereference-recursive   Recurse and follow symbolic links.
      --include=GLOB            Search file names matching GLOB.
      --exclude=GLOB            Skip file names matching GLOB.
      --exclude-from=FILE       Read exclusion patterns from FILE.
      --exclude-dir=GLOB        Skip directories matching GLOB.
  -L, --files-without-match     List files without a selection.
  -l, --files-with-matches      List files with a selection.
  -c, --count                   Print the selection count per file.
  -T, --initial-tab             Align the text after output prefixes.
  -Z, --null                    End file name prefixes with NUL.

Context control:
  -B, --before-context=NUM      Show NUM preceding lines.
  -A, --after-context=NUM       Show NUM following lines.
  -C, --context=NUM             Show NUM lines on each side.
  -NUM                          Short form of --context=NUM.
      --group-separator=SEP     Separate context groups with SEP.
      --no-group-separator      Omit separators between context groups.
      --color[=WHEN], --colour[=WHEN]
                                Highlight matches: always, never or auto.
  -U, --binary                  Select binary I/O mode.

Read standard input when FILE is '-'. With no file operand, read stdin
or search the current directory when recursion is requested.
Exit status: 0 for a match, 1 for none, 2 for an error.
With -q, a match returns 0 even after an input error.
